logicgates.learning.componentResult = {module}: found {actual}; required {required} — {result}
logicgates.learning.unrestricted = unrestricted
logicgates.learning.checkMatch = Correct
logicgates.learning.checkMismatch = Mismatch
logicgates.learning.checkUnstable = Inconclusive: unresolved feedback
logicgates.learning.checkDisconnected = Inconclusive: disconnected input/output
logicgates.learning.portOrder = Inputs I and outputs O use local submission coordinates (X, Y, Z), sorted by X, then Y, then Z. Only the circuit inside the submitted area is evaluated.
logicgates.learning.countsOnly = No published table: only quantities were checked. Grading remains manual.
logicgates.learning.ioMismatch = Table not executed: the lever or lamp count differs from the expected inputs/outputs. Check the components and statement.
logicgates.learning.caseSummary = Behavior: {passed} of {total} cases correct.
logicgates.learning.caseResult = {inputs} -> expected {expected}; found {actual} — {result}
logicgates.learning.manualGradeNotice = Analysis uses the fixed submitted copy. Inconclusive cases are not a zero grade. The teacher still decides the score.
logicgates.learning.error.INVALID_RULES = Check quantities (0 to 16384) and the complete table without duplicate combinations. Use inputs -> outputs with 1 to 6 inputs and 1 to 4 outputs; lever/lamp requirements must match the table.
logicgates.learning.error.VERIFICATION_LIMIT = Logical verification supports up to 2048 logical components, 6 levers and 4 lamps. The submission remains available for manual review.
